+.SH Session management
+If \fB\-R\fP is given, w3m will restore a session from a session file.
+If no session file is provided with \fB\-session\fR the default session file
+is used. The default session file will be deleted after restoring a session
+when exiting w3m.
+
+Without a given session file, when manually storing a session, w3m will ask
+for a filename.
+
+If a session file is given, it will not be deleted and will be overwritten if
+storing a session again.
+
+Automatic session storing and restoring can be configured via the options.
+
 .SH EXAMPLES
 .SS Pager-like usage
 .TP
